{"id":600,"date":"2016-04-11T07:53:14","date_gmt":"2016-04-11T12:53:14","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/herbbaldwin.wordpress.com\/?p=600"},"modified":"2016-04-11T07:53:14","modified_gmt":"2016-04-11T12:53:14","slug":"visiting-the-alamo-dale-miller","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/2016\/04\/11\/visiting-the-alamo-dale-miller\/","title":{"rendered":"Visiting the Alamo &amp; Dale Miller"},"content":{"rendered":"<p>Having left <a href=\"https:\/\/www.escapees.com\/parking\/rainbow-parks\/livingston-texas\" target=\"_blank\">Rainbow&#8217;s End Escapee RV Park<\/a> in Lewiston, TX on Sunday morning we headed (without incident!) on down I-35 and then west on I-10 over to <a href=\"http:\/\/www.riverbendrvpark.com\/\" target=\"_blank\">RiverBend RV Park<\/a> in Luling, TX, about an hour east of San Antonio.<\/p>\n<p>When we got in about 3pm on Sunday we parked and then right away called our old friend Dale Miller. \u00a0Dale and I were Realtors at the same time at the Coldwell Banker office in Delaware back 10+ years ago. \u00a0We wanted to try to meet Dale for dinner.<\/p>\n<p>We took the car another hour west on into San Antonio and the Alamo where Dale works as a Texas Ranger. \u00a0Although he had just finished his shift for the day, he graciously provided us with a free parking spot and a private guided tour of the Alamo buildings and grounds.<\/p>\n<p>While visiting most museums, it&#8217;s left to the visitor to read all the little signs, Dale did the interpreting for us and his stories were interesting and informative and even entertaining!<\/p>\n<p>Then the three of us headed on over to the Riverwalk and enjoyed dinner together at <a href=\"http:\/\/www.thesanantonioriverwalk.com\/directory\/county-line\" target=\"_blank\">County Line BBQ<\/a>, afterwards taking a short walk along the river.<\/p>\n<div id='gallery-1' class='gallery galleryid-600 gallery-columns-3 gallery-size-thumbnail'><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/04\/2016-04-10-16-25-33.jpg'><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/04\/2016-04-10-16-25-33-150x150.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"\" \/><\/a>\n\t\t\t<\/div><\/figure><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/04\/2016-04-10-16-48-23.jpg'><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/04\/2016-04-10-16-48-23-150x150.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"\" \/><\/a>\n\t\t\t<\/div><\/figure><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/04\/2016-04-10-19-35-53.jpg'><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/04\/2016-04-10-19-35-53-150x150.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"\" \/><\/a>\n\t\t\t<\/div><\/figure><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/04\/2016-04-10-19-27-46.jpg'><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/04\/2016-04-10-19-27-46-150x150.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"\" \/><\/a>\n\t\t\t<\/div><\/figure>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\n<p>Back at Riverbend for the night, in the morning we&#8217;ll take a walk back to the San Marcos River at the back of the campground, very likely visit San Antonio again, and we&#8217;ve been told we need to drive up to hill country about an hour to the north to <a href=\"http:\/\/www.fredericksburgtexas-online.com\/\" target=\"_blank\">Fredericksburg<\/a>.<\/p>\n<p>We&#8217;ll post more later, stay tuned.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Having left Rainbow&#8217;s End Escapee RV Park in Lewiston, TX on Sunday morning we headed (without incident!) on down I-35 and then west on I-10 over to RiverBend RV Park in Luling, TX, about an hour east of San Antonio. When we got in about 3pm on Sunday we parked and then right away called &hellip; <a href=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/2016\/04\/11\/visiting-the-alamo-dale-miller\/\" class=\"more-link\">Continue reading <span class=\"screen-reader-text\">Visiting the Alamo &amp; Dale Miller<\/span><\/a><\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":0,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"footnotes":""},"categories":[586,19546],"tags":[555305,110088,1192622],"class_list":["post-600","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","hentry","category-food","category-sightseeing","tag-alamo","tag-bbq","tag-riverwalk"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/600","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/post"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/1"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=600"}],"version-history":[{"count":25,"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/600\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":631,"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/600\/revisions\/631"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=600"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/categories?post=600"},{"taxonomy":"post_tag","embeddable":true,"h